  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "The numbers \\(16\\) and \\(25\\) are a pair of consecutive positive perfect squares whose difference is \\(9.\\) How many pairs of consecutive positive perfect squares have a difference of less than or equal to \\(2023?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
