  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2023-p9.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Consecutive squares \\(k^2\\) and \\((k+1)^2\\) differ by \\((k+1)^2 - k^2 = 2k + 1.\\) We need \\(2k + 1 \\le 2023,\\) which gives \\(k \\le 1011.\\) So \\(k\\) runs \\(1, 2, \\ldots, 1011,\\) for \\(1011\\) pairs. Thus, B is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Consecutive squares \\(k^2\\) and \\((k+1)^2\\) differ by \\(2k+1\\)",
        "Solve \\(2k + 1 \\le 2023\\) for positive integers \\(k\\)"
      ],
